tonatools.git.remoteTemplates.markdownDescription:
URL templates per git remote host, used by `Git: Copy file location in remote url`.

`github.com`, `gitlab.com` and `bitbucket.org` are built in. Keys you leave out fall back individually, most specific first: your entry for the host, then the built-in for that host, then your `*` entry, then the default — so you only write the keys that differ. Use `*` as the host to override the fallback for unrecognised hosts.

```json
{
  "git.example.com": {
    "file": "https://${host}/${path}/-/blob/${branch}/${file}",
    "line": "#L${start}",
    "lineRange": "#L${start}-${end}"
  }
}
```
